resolve - a name to its address, and where the answer came from

  resolve www.example.com
  resolve printer.lan builder.lan

Each name prints its address and its source: the hosts file, or DNS
with the time the servers took. Anything networked asks names the
same way, so this command is how the path is inspected when a name
misbehaves.

The file /etc/hosts answers before any server is asked. One line per
address, names after it, `#` comments:

  192.0.2.10   builder builder.lan

DNS servers come from the DHCP lease, or from a `dns` entry in the
interface's configuration, which outranks the lease. `cfg net` shows
what is recorded.
